      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we first need to determine the number of terms in the sequence and then calculate the sum of these terms. Finally, we will find the remainder when this sum is divided by 6.\n\n1. **Identify the sequence and the number of terms:**\n   The sequence given is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). The last term \\(l = 259\\).\n\n   The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   Setting \\(a_n = 259\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\implies 259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\implies 259 = 6n - 5 \\implies 264 = 6n \\implies n = 44\n   \\]\n   So, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\n2. **Calculate the sum of the sequence:**\n   The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the remainder when the sum is divided by 6:**\n   To find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6, we can use the property that \\((a \\cdot b) \\mod m = [(a \\mod m) \\cdot (b \\mod m)] \\mod m\\). First, we find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6.\n   \\[\n   5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\implies 5720 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{6}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
