      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we start by identifying the sequence and its properties. The given sequence is an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common difference \\(d = 6\\).\n\nFirst, we need to find the number of terms in the sequence. The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d\\]\nWe set \\(a_n = 259\\) to find \\(n\\):\n\\[259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\\]\n\\[259 = 1 + 6n - 6\\]\n\\[259 = 6n - 5\\]\n\\[264 = 6n\\]\n\\[n = 44\\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nNext, we need to find the sum of the sequence. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Here, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\):\n\\[S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by calculating the remainder of 5720 when divided by 6:\n\\[5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2.\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
